IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg2-support`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1: section 141(c) -- COMMITTEES OF THE BOARD AND THEIR SUBCOMMITTEES.
--
-- Two paragraphs, (c)(1) and (c)(2), cover committees; which one governs depends on the date of incorporation and on a
-- resolution of the whole board. Paragraph (c)(3) lets a committee create subcommittees; paragraph (c)(4) fixes the quorum and
-- the act of a committee. SEAT: a director (or a stockholder) asking what a committee may do. The text is
-- de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (a plain-text rendering, not the official text). Cross-references taken as inputs:
-- section 151(a) (piece dg3), sections 251 to 264 (pieces dg6 to dg8), section 253 (piece dg6).
-- Counts of directors are counts of votes where the certificate gives a director more or less than one vote (s 141(d), src:369).

§ `Section 141(c): which paragraph governs the corporation`

-- "All corporations incorporated prior to July 1, 1996" and "on or after July 1, 1996": the two cover every date.
-- src:365 | All corporations incorporated prior to July 1, 1996, shall be governed by this paragraph (c)(1) of this section, provided that any such corporation may by a resolution adopted by a majority of the whole board elect to be governed by paragraph (c)(2) of this section, in which case this paragraph (c)(1) of this section shall not apply to such corporation. All corporations incorporated on or after July 1, 1996, shall be governed by paragraph (c)(2) of this section. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(c)(1) (src:365)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 141(c)(1) July 1, 1996` MEANS YearMonthDay 1996 7 1

-- src:365 | All corporations incorporated prior to July 1, 1996, shall be governed by this paragraph (c)(1) of this section, provided that any such corporation may by a resolution adopted by a majority of the whole board elect to be governed by paragraph (c)(2) of this section, in which case this paragraph (c)(1) of this section shall not apply to such corporation. All corporations incorporated on or after July 1, 1996, shall be governed by paragraph (c)(2) of this section. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(c)(1) (src:365)
DECLARE `s 141(c) Paragraph that governs the corporation` IS ONE OF
    `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation`
    `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation`

-- A corporation incorporated before 1 July 1996 is governed by (c)(1) unless a resolution adopted by a majority of the whole board
-- elected (c)(2). A corporation incorporated on or after that date is governed by (c)(2). NOTHING when the votes cannot be a vote.
-- src:365 | All corporations incorporated prior to July 1, 1996, shall be governed by this paragraph (c)(1) of this section, provided that any such corporation may by a resolution adopted by a majority of the whole board elect to be governed by paragraph (c)(2) of this section, in which case this paragraph (c)(1) of this section shall not apply to such corporation. All corporations incorporated on or after July 1, 1996, shall be governed by paragraph (c)(2) of this section. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(c)(1) (src:365)
GIVEN `the date the corporation was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the number of directors on the whole board` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of the whole board who adopted a resolution electing paragraph (c)(2)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 141(c) Paragraph that governs the corporation`
`s 141(c) which paragraph governs the corporation` `the date the corporation was incorporated` `the number of directors on the whole board` `the number of the whole board who adopted a resolution electing paragraph (c)(2)` MEANS
    IF   `the date the corporation was incorporated` AT LEAST `s 141(c)(1) July 1, 1996`
    THEN JUST `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the number of the whole board who adopted a resolution electing paragraph (c)(2)`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation`
         WHEN JUST v THEN
             CONSIDER `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the whole board`) v `the number of directors on the whole board`
             WHEN JUST carried THEN (IF carried
                                     THEN JUST `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation`
                                     ELSE JUST `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation`)
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§ `Section 141(c): designating committees and their members`

-- (c)(1): "The board of directors may, by resolution passed by a majority of the whole board, designate 1 or more committees,
-- each committee to consist of 1 or more of the directors of the corporation."
-- src:365 | The board of directors may, by resolution passed by a majority of the whole board, designate 1 or more committees, each committee to consist of 1 or more of the directors of the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(c)(1) (src:365)
GIVEN `the number of directors on the whole board` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of the whole board who passed the resolution` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors on the committee` IS A NUMBER
      `every member of the committee is a director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141(c)(1) the board may designate the committee` `the number of directors on the whole board` `the number of the whole board who passed the resolution` `the number of directors on the committee` `every member of the committee is a director of the corporation` MEANS
    `dg2 both findings hold`
        (`the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the whole board`) `the number of the whole board who passed the resolution` `the number of directors on the whole board`)
        (JUST ((`the number of directors on the committee` AT LEAST 1) AND `every member of the committee is a director of the corporation`))

-- (c)(2): "The board of directors may designate 1 or more committees, each committee to consist of 1 or more of the directors of
-- the corporation." No vote is stated, so the ordinary act of the board under s 141(b) is what the board needs.
-- src:366 | The board of directors may designate 1 or more committees, each committee to consist of 1 or more of the directors of the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(c)(2) (src:366)
GIVEN `the board acted by the vote that section 141(b) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of directors on the committee` IS A NUMBER
      `every member of the committee is a director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(c)(2) the board may designate the committee` `the board acted by the vote that section 141(b) requires` `the number of directors on the committee` `every member of the committee is a director of the corporation` MEANS
        `the board acted by the vote that section 141(b) requires`
    AND (`the number of directors on the committee` AT LEAST 1)
    AND `every member of the committee is a director of the corporation`

-- "The board may designate 1 or more directors as alternate members of any committee, who may replace any absent or disqualified
-- member at any meeting of the committee." (the same sentence in (c)(1) and (c)(2))
-- src:365 | The board may designate 1 or more directors as alternate members of any committee, who may replace any absent or disqualified member at any meeting of the committee. …
-- src:366 | The board may designate 1 or more directors as alternate members of any committee, who may replace any absent or disqualified member at any meeting of the committee. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(c)(1) (src:365); § 141(c)(2) (src:366)
GIVEN `the board designated the person as an alternate member of the committee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member is absent or disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(c) an alternate member may replace the member at the meeting` `the board designated the person as an alternate member of the committee` `the person is a director of the corporation` `the member is absent or disqualified` MEANS
        `the board designated the person as an alternate member of the committee`
    AND `the person is a director of the corporation`
    AND `the member is absent or disqualified`

-- "The bylaws may provide that in the absence or disqualification of a member of a committee, the member or members present at
-- any meeting and not disqualified from voting, whether or not the member or members present constitute a quorum, may
-- unanimously appoint another member of the board of directors to act at the meeting in the place of any such absent or
-- disqualified member."
-- src:365 | The bylaws may provide that in the absence or disqualification of a member of a committee, the member or members present at any meeting and not disqualified from voting, whether or not the member or members present constitute a quorum, may unanimously appoint another member of the board of directors to act at the meeting in the place of any such absent or disqualified member. …
-- src:366 | The bylaws may provide that in the absence or disqualification of a member of a committee, the member or members present at any meeting and not disqualified from voting, whether or not such member or members constitute a quorum, may unanimously appoint another member of the board of directors to act at the meeting in the place of any such absent or disqualified member. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(c)(1) (src:365); § 141(c)(2) (src:366)
GIVEN `the bylaws so provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the members present and not disqualified from voting appoint unanimously` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person appointed is a member of the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(c) the members present may appoint another director to act in place of the absent member` `the bylaws so provide` `the members present and not disqualified from voting appoint unanimously` `the person appointed is a member of the board of directors` MEANS
        `the bylaws so provide`
    AND `the members present and not disqualified from voting appoint unanimously`
    AND `the person appointed is a member of the board of directors`

§ `Section 141(c): what a committee may do`

-- The matters the two paragraphs name. Under (c)(1) the list is the first group (and the third, which needs an express
-- provision); under (c)(2) it is the second group. Every other matter is within the committee's power "to the extent provided in
-- the resolution of the board of directors, or in the bylaws".
-- src:365 | Any such committee, to the extent provided in the resolution of the board of directors, or in the bylaws of the corporation, shall have and may exercise all the powers and authority of the board of directors in the management of the business and affairs of the corporation, and may authorize the seal of the corporation to be affixed to all papers which may require it; but no such committee shall have the power or authority in reference to amending the certificate of incorporation (except that a committee may, to the extent authorized in the resolution or resolutions providing for the issuance of shares of stock adopted by the board of directors as provided in § 151(a) of this title, fix the designations and any of the preferences or rights of such shares relating to dividends, redemption, dissolution, any distribution of assets of the corporation or the conversion into, or the exchange of such shares for, shares of any other class or classes or any other series of the same or any other class or classes of stock of the corporation or fix the number of shares of any series of stock or authorize the increase or decrease of the shares of any series), adopting an agreement of merger or consolidation under § 251, § 252, § 254, § 255, § 256, § 257, § 258, § 263 or § 264 of this title, recommending to the stockholders the sale, lease or exchange of all or substantially all of the corporation’s property and assets, recommending to the stockholders a dissolution of the corporation or a revocation of a dissolution, or amending the bylaws of the corporation; and, unless the resolution, bylaws or certificate of incorporation expressly so provides, no such committee shall have the power or authority to declare a dividend, to authorize the issuance of stock or to adopt a certificate of ownership and merger pursuant to § 253 of this title.
-- src:366 | Any such committee, to the extent provided in the resolution of the board of directors, or in the bylaws of the corporation, shall have and may exercise all the powers and authority of the board of directors in the management of the business and affairs of the corporation, and may authorize the seal of the corporation to be affixed to all papers which may require it; but no such committee shall have the power or authority in reference to the following matter: (i) approving or adopting, or recommending to the stockholders, any action or matter (other than the election or removal of directors) expressly required by this chapter to be submitted to stockholders for approval or (ii) adopting, amending or repealing any bylaw of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(c)(1) (src:365); § 141(c)(2) (src:366)
DECLARE `s 141(c) Matter before a committee` IS ONE OF
    `amending the certificate of incorporation, otherwise than by fixing the terms of shares under a resolution adopted as provided in s 151(a)`
-- out of range: section 151(a) (piece dg3): the board resolution that fixes the terms of a series is taken as the name of the matter.
    `fixing the designations and preferences or rights of shares, or the number of shares of a series, or authorizing an increase or decrease in them, under a resolution adopted by the board as provided in s 151(a)`
-- out of range: sections 251, 252 and 254 (piece dg6), 255 to 258 (piece dg7), 263 and 264 (piece dg8): the sections are named by subsection (c)(1) and are taken as the name of the matter, not read.
    `adopting an agreement of merger or consolidation under s 251, 252, 254, 255, 256, 257, 258, 263 or 264`
    `adopting an agreement of merger or consolidation under a section other than those s 141(c)(1) lists`
    `recommending to the stockholders the sale, lease or exchange of all or substantially all of the corporation's property and assets`
    `recommending to the stockholders a dissolution of the corporation or a revocation of a dissolution`
    `amending a bylaw of the corporation`
    `adopting a bylaw of the corporation`
    `repealing a bylaw of the corporation`
    `declaring a dividend`
    `authorizing the issuance of stock`
-- out of range: section 253 (piece dg6): named by subsection (c)(1); taken as the name of the matter, not read.
    `adopting a certificate of ownership and merger pursuant to s 253`
    `approving or adopting, or recommending to the stockholders, an action or matter expressly required by this chapter to be submitted to stockholders for approval`
    `approving or recommending the election or removal of directors`
    `any other matter in the management of the business and affairs of the corporation`

DECLARE `s 141(c) What the board or the bylaws gave the committee` HAS
    `the resolution of the board of directors or the bylaws provide that the committee has and may exercise the power of the board` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the resolution, the bylaws or the certificate of incorporation expressly provide that the committee may do the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
-- out of range: section 151(a) (piece dg3): whether the committee acts within a resolution adopted as provided there is a plain input.
    `the committee acts to the extent authorized in a resolution providing for the issuance of shares adopted by the board as provided in s 151(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
-- out of range: the sections of this chapter that submit a matter to stockholders (pieces dg3 to dg11): whether this chapter so requires for the matter is one plain input.
    `this chapter expressly requires the matter to be submitted to stockholders for approval` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Does the committee have the power in the matter? Under (c)(1): none over amending the certificate (save the share terms, which need the
-- s 151(a) authority), mergers under the listed sections, recommending a sale of all or substantially all assets or a dissolution,
-- or amending the bylaws; and none to declare a dividend, authorize the issuance of stock or adopt a s 253 certificate unless
-- expressly provided. Under (c)(2): none over approving or recommending a matter required to be submitted to stockholders
-- (other than the election or removal of directors) or over adopting, amending or repealing a bylaw. The text names only
-- "amending" the bylaws in (c)(1): whether a committee under (c)(1) may adopt or repeal a bylaw it does not say: NOTHING.
-- Under (c)(2) the bar on a matter "expressly required by this chapter to be submitted to stockholders for approval" is applied
-- by a fact the person states (whether the chapter so requires), so that a certificate amendment, a merger, a sale of assets or a
-- dissolution, each of which the chapter submits to stockholders, is barred without a list of sections (Fork F-141-4).
-- src:365 | Any such committee, to the extent provided in the resolution of the board of directors, or in the bylaws of the corporation, shall have and may exercise all the powers and authority of the board of directors in the management of the business and affairs of the corporation, and may authorize the seal of the corporation to be affixed to all papers which may require it; but no such committee shall have the power or authority in reference to amending the certificate of incorporation (except that a committee may, to the extent authorized in the resolution or resolutions providing for the issuance of shares of stock adopted by the board of directors as provided in § 151(a) of this title, fix the designations and any of the preferences or rights of such shares relating to dividends, redemption, dissolution, any distribution of assets of the corporation or the conversion into, or the exchange of such shares for, shares of any other class or classes or any other series of the same or any other class or classes of stock of the corporation or fix the number of shares of any series of stock or authorize the increase or decrease of the shares of any series), adopting an agreement of merger or consolidation under § 251, § 252, § 254, § 255, § 256, § 257, § 258, § 263 or § 264 of this title, recommending to the stockholders the sale, lease or exchange of all or substantially all of the corporation’s property and assets, recommending to the stockholders a dissolution of the corporation or a revocation of a dissolution, or amending the bylaws of the corporation; and, unless the resolution, bylaws or certificate of incorporation expressly so provides, no such committee shall have the power or authority to declare a dividend, to authorize the issuance of stock or to adopt a certificate of ownership and merger pursuant to § 253 of this title.
-- src:366 | Any such committee, to the extent provided in the resolution of the board of directors, or in the bylaws of the corporation, shall have and may exercise all the powers and authority of the board of directors in the management of the business and affairs of the corporation, and may authorize the seal of the corporation to be affixed to all papers which may require it; but no such committee shall have the power or authority in reference to the following matter: (i) approving or adopting, or recommending to the stockholders, any action or matter (other than the election or removal of directors) expressly required by this chapter to be submitted to stockholders for approval or (ii) adopting, amending or repealing any bylaw of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(c)(1) (src:365); § 141(c)(2) (src:366)
GIVEN `the paragraph that governs` IS A `s 141(c) Paragraph that governs the corporation`
      `the matter` IS A `s 141(c) Matter before a committee`
      `what was given` IS A `s 141(c) What the board or the bylaws gave the committee`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `the paragraph that governs` `the matter` `what was given` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the paragraph that governs`
    WHEN `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` THEN
        CONSIDER `the matter`
        WHEN `amending the certificate of incorporation, otherwise than by fixing the terms of shares under a resolution adopted as provided in s 151(a)` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `fixing the designations and preferences or rights of shares, or the number of shares of a series, or authorizing an increase or decrease in them, under a resolution adopted by the board as provided in s 151(a)` THEN
            JUST (provided AND authorized)
        WHEN `adopting an agreement of merger or consolidation under s 251, 252, 254, 255, 256, 257, 258, 263 or 264` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `recommending to the stockholders the sale, lease or exchange of all or substantially all of the corporation's property and assets` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `recommending to the stockholders a dissolution of the corporation or a revocation of a dissolution` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `amending a bylaw of the corporation` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `adopting a bylaw of the corporation` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `repealing a bylaw of the corporation` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `declaring a dividend` THEN JUST (provided AND expressly)
        WHEN `authorizing the issuance of stock` THEN JUST (provided AND expressly)
        WHEN `adopting a certificate of ownership and merger pursuant to s 253` THEN JUST (provided AND expressly)
        OTHERWISE JUST provided
    WHEN `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation` THEN
        CONSIDER `the matter`
        WHEN `approving or adopting, or recommending to the stockholders, an action or matter expressly required by this chapter to be submitted to stockholders for approval` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `amending a bylaw of the corporation` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `adopting a bylaw of the corporation` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `repealing a bylaw of the corporation` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `approving or recommending the election or removal of directors` THEN JUST provided
        OTHERWISE JUST (provided AND (NOT submitted))
    WHERE
        provided MEANS `what was given`'s `the resolution of the board of directors or the bylaws provide that the committee has and may exercise the power of the board`
        expressly MEANS `what was given`'s `the resolution, the bylaws or the certificate of incorporation expressly provide that the committee may do the thing`
        authorized MEANS `what was given`'s `the committee acts to the extent authorized in a resolution providing for the issuance of shares adopted by the board as provided in s 151(a)`
        submitted MEANS `what was given`'s `this chapter expressly requires the matter to be submitted to stockholders for approval`

§ `Section 141(c)(3): subcommittees`

-- "Unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws or the resolution of the board of directors
-- designating the committee, a committee may create 1 or more subcommittees, each subcommittee to consist of 1 or more members
-- of the committee, and delegate to a subcommittee any or all of the powers and authority of the committee."
-- src:367 | Unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws or the resolution of the board of directors designating the committee, a committee may create 1 or more subcommittees, each subcommittee to consist of 1 or more members of the committee, and delegate to a subcommittee any or all of the powers and authority of the committee. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(c)(3) (src:367)
GIVEN `where it is otherwise provided` IS A `Where a provision is made`
      `the number of members of the committee on the subcommittee` IS A NUMBER
      `every member of the subcommittee is a member of the committee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(c)(3) the committee may create the subcommittee and delegate its powers to it` `where it is otherwise provided` `the number of members of the committee on the subcommittee` `every member of the subcommittee is a member of the committee` MEANS
        `where it is otherwise provided` EQUALS `in none of these`
    AND (`the number of members of the committee on the subcommittee` AT LEAST 1)
    AND `every member of the subcommittee is a member of the committee`

-- "Except for references to committees and members of committees in subsection (c) of this section, every reference in this
-- chapter to a committee of the board of directors or a member of a committee shall be deemed to include a reference to a
-- subcommittee or member of a subcommittee." The deeming rule: a reference elsewhere in the chapter includes subcommittees; a
-- reference inside subsection (c) does not.
-- src:367 | Except for references to committees and members of committees in subsection (c) of this section, every reference in this chapter to a committee of the board of directors or a member of a committee shall be deemed to include a reference to a subcommittee or member of a subcommittee.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(c)(3) (src:367)
GIVEN `the reference is in subsection (c) of section 141` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(c)(3) a reference to a committee includes a subcommittee` `the reference is in subsection (c) of section 141` MEANS
    NOT `the reference is in subsection (c) of section 141`

§ `Section 141(c)(4): the quorum and the act of a committee or subcommittee`

-- The places where a quorum or a vote may be fixed for a committee or subcommittee: the certificate, the bylaws, a resolution of
-- the board, or a resolution of the committee that created the subcommittee. The core's `Where a provision is made` lacks the last.
-- src:368 | unless the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws, a resolution of the board of directors or a resolution of a committee that created the subcommittee requires a greater or lesser number …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(c)(4) (src:368)
DECLARE `s 141(c)(4) Where the committee's number is fixed` IS ONE OF
    `in the certificate of incorporation, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`
    `in the bylaws, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`
    `in a resolution of the board of directors, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`
    `in a resolution of the committee that created the subcommittee, under s 141(c)(4)`
    `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`

GIVEN w IS A `s 141(c)(4) Where the committee's number is fixed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(c)(4) the place is one the text recognises` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE `s 141(c)(4) Committee provisions` HAS
    `the number of directors then serving on the committee or subcommittee` IS A NUMBER
    `the number fixed as a quorum` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `where the quorum is fixed` IS A `s 141(c)(4) Where the committee's number is fixed`
    `the number of members who must vote in favor, if a greater number is fixed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `where the greater vote is fixed` IS A `s 141(c)(4) Where the committee's number is fixed`

-- "A majority of the directors then serving on a committee ... shall constitute a quorum ..., unless the certificate of incorporation,
-- the bylaws, a resolution of the board of directors or a resolution of a committee that created the subcommittee requires a greater
-- or lesser number, provided that in no case shall a quorum be less than 1/3 of the directors then serving on the committee or
-- subcommittee." A number fixed in a recognised place is the quorum if it is at least one third and at most the number serving;
-- below one third, or above the number serving, the text does not say what the quorum is: NOTHING.
-- src:368 | A majority of the directors then serving on a committee of the board of directors or on a subcommittee of a committee shall constitute a quorum for the transaction of business by the committee or subcommittee, unless the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws, a resolution of the board of directors or a resolution of a committee that created the subcommittee requires a greater or lesser number, provided that in no case shall a quorum be less than ⅓ of the directors then serving on the committee or subcommittee. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(c)(4) (src:368)
GIVEN c IS A `s 141(c)(4) Committee provisions`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Vote requirement`
`s 141(c)(4) the quorum requirement` c MEANS
    IF   c's `the number of directors then serving on the committee or subcommittee` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER c's `the number fixed as a quorum`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`a majority of` `the directors then serving on a committee`)
         WHEN JUST k THEN
             BRANCH
                 IF   NOT (`s 141(c)(4) the place is one the text recognises` (c's `where the quorum is fixed`))
                 THEN JUST (`a majority of` `the directors then serving on a committee`)
                 IF   (k AT MOST c's `the number of directors then serving on the committee or subcommittee`)
                      AND (k AT LEAST (c's `the number of directors then serving on the committee or subcommittee` DIVIDED BY 3))
                 THEN JUST (`at least` (k DIVIDED BY c's `the number of directors then serving on the committee or subcommittee`) `of` `the directors then serving on a committee`)
                 OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:368 | A majority of the directors then serving on a committee of the board of directors or on a subcommittee of a committee shall constitute a quorum for the transaction of business by the committee or subcommittee, unless the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws, a resolution of the board of directors or a resolution of a committee that created the subcommittee requires a greater or lesser number, provided that in no case shall a quorum be less than ⅓ of the directors then serving on the committee or subcommittee. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(c)(4) (src:368)
GIVEN `the number of members present` IS A NUMBER
      c IS A `s 141(c)(4) Committee provisions`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141(c)(4) a quorum of the committee is present` `the number of members present` c MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 141(c)(4) the quorum requirement` c
    WHEN JUST r THEN `the vote carries` r `the number of members present` (c's `the number of directors then serving on the committee or subcommittee`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- "The vote of the majority of the members of a committee or subcommittee present at a meeting at which a quorum is present shall
-- be the act of the committee or subcommittee, unless the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws, a resolution of the board of
-- directors or a resolution of a committee that created the subcommittee requires a greater number."
-- src:368 | The vote of the majority of the members of a committee or subcommittee present at a meeting at which a quorum is present shall be the act of the committee or subcommittee, unless the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws, a resolution of the board of directors or a resolution of a committee that created the subcommittee requires a greater number.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(c)(4) (src:368)
GIVEN `the number of members present` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members voting in favor` IS A NUMBER
      c IS A `s 141(c)(4) Committee provisions`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141(c)(4) the act of the committee is carried` `the number of members present` `the number of members voting in favor` c MEANS
    `dg2 both findings hold`
        (`s 141(c)(4) a quorum of the committee is present` `the number of members present` c)
        (`dg2 both findings hold`
            (`the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the directors present at a meeting at which a quorum is present`) `the number of members voting in favor` `the number of members present`)
            (CONSIDER c's `the number of members who must vote in favor, if a greater number is fixed`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN JUST n THEN
                 (IF   `s 141(c)(4) the place is one the text recognises` (c's `where the greater vote is fixed`)
                  THEN JUST (`the number of members voting in favor` AT LEAST n)
                  ELSE JUST TRUE)))
